## Context
Prose review panel 2026-06-11 (pre-arXiv), three factual inconsistencies that
block submission. Imagine-phase fact check (2026-06-11) against committed
artifacts established the ground truth below; the remaining work is small
prose fixes plus one derivation.

1. **Wikipedia seeding attribution inconsistency.** Body line ~97 says "an
   intern in the author's group injected reference-derived content" (19 June
   2019, revision 902510278); COI line ~547 says "the author ... also authored
   the Wikipedia pages for several of the plants." Intern vs author — one is
   wrong. Make the two passages consistent; final factual confirmation rests
   with the author at PR review. Note: abstract/conclusion do NOT currently
   over-extrapolate seeded recall to all 177 plants (conclusion correctly says
   "92% of the built fleet") — any residual claim-strength concern there
   belongs to ticket 0532, not here.
2. **GEM "119 distinct plants" vs "157 of 177 matched" — apparent
   contradiction, actually a grain difference.** Line ~246: gem_thermal.csv
   has 153 rows, 119 distinct plant names. Line ~248: tab_source_concordance.csv
   confirms 157 reference plants found a GEM match — many-to-one matching, one
   GEM plant row can match multiple reference phase rows. Fix: one explanatory
   clause. Also pin the GEM snapshot date (PROVENANCE.md line ~298 admits "the
   export date and URL are not stamped" — recover best-known date from git
   history of gem_units.csv).
3. **Refusals wording — cohort confusion.** Line ~99 "all produced usable
   tables" is TRUE for the reported cohort (exp1_batch2: all 70 runs
   status="ok"; GPT-5.5 all 5 runs F1 0.61–0.65, no refusals). Line ~101
   "GPT-5.5 declines the task on 3 of its 5 reps" describes the ARCHIVED
   baseline sweep (experiments/archive/outputs/exp1/baseline/, prompt p1_base),
   not the current cohort. As written the two lines contradict each other.
   Fix: attribute the refusal anecdote explicitly to the archived baseline
   ("In an earlier sweep (archived baseline, prompt p1_base), GPT-5.5 declined
   3 of 5 reps ..."), note the batch2 re-run resolved compliance, and report
   refusal rate + conditional F1 on completing runs — all numbers derived by
   script from the archive record files, never typed from a survey. The author
   may instead cut the paragraph at PR review; the PR proposes the attribution
   fix as the default since it preserves the reported-numbers exit criterion.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — lines ~97, ~99, ~101, ~246–248, ~547 (COI)
- `experiments/outputs/exp1_batch2/gpt-5.5-run*.record.json` — current cohort, no refusals
- `experiments/archive/outputs/exp1/baseline/gpt-5.5-run*.json` / `.record.json` — refusal evidence (runs 1,3,5 refused; run 2 F1=0.64; run 4 F1=0.0 n_plants=1)
- `data/reference/gem_thermal.csv` — 153 rows, 119 distinct plant names
- `data/reference/tab_source_concordance.csv` — 157 gem_matched
- `data/reference/gem_units.csv` + `data/reference/PROVENANCE.md` (~lines 294–337) — GEM snapshot, date not stamped

## Actions
1. Seeding attribution: align line ~97 (body) and line ~547 (COI) on one
   consistent account. The body's intern account is the more specific
   (named revision, date); adjust the COI wording to match it unless project
   records contradict — flag the chosen account prominently in the PR body
   for author confirmation.
2. GEM counts: (a) add a clause at line ~248 explaining 157-vs-119 as
   phase-grain matching (one GEM plant row can match several reference phase
   rows); (b) pin the GEM snapshot date from
   `git log --diff-filter=A -- data/reference/gem_units.csv` (or PROVENANCE
   best-known date) into the prose and/or PROVENANCE.md.
3. Refusals: rewrite lines ~99–101 so the refusal anecdote is attributed to
   the archived baseline sweep; derive refusal rate and conditional F1 from
   the archive files with a small throwaway derivation (committed evidence
   path quoted in prose or PR body), per the derive-from-artifacts rule.

## Test
- Numbers introduced by fix 3 (refusal rate, conditional F1) derive from
  committed artifacts (or land as macros if 0531 has shipped).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Seeding attribution consistent between body and COI; author confirms facts.
- [ ] GEM count discrepancy explained or corrected; GEM release version pinned.
- [ ] Refusals wording accurate; conditional F1 + refusal rate reported.
